{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-0240"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Support Services To Forestry Coordination"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "0240"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :forestry/support-services
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:forest-health :fire-risk-reduction :contract-labor-efficiency]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :forestrysupport-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics false
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:identity :forms :audit-ledger]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies [:telemetry]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "ForestrySupportAdvisor (`forestrysupport.advisor`) ⊣ Forestry-Support
 Operations Governor (`forestrysupport.governor`), composed by
 `forestrysupport.operation/build` into a REAL compiled `langgraph-clj`
 StateGraph (`langgraph.graph`, `state-graph`/`add-node`/
 `add-conditional-edges`/`compile-graph`): `:intake -> :advise -> :govern
 -> :decide -+-> :commit / :request-approval -> :commit / :hold`, with
 `interrupt-before #{:request-approval}` + in-memory checkpointer for
 real human-in-the-loop resume. Append-only audit ledger
 (`forestrysupport.store/ledger` + `append-ledger!`, `MemStore`) is wired
 into the compiled graph's own `:commit` and `:hold` nodes.

 Fixes THREE compounding gaps found in the prior scaffold (2026-07-16,
 `c34cd28`): (1) `deps.edn` declared the real
 `io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph` coordinate only inside the `:dev`
 alias's `:override-deps`, which REPLACES an already-present dependency
 rather than adding one -- with base `:deps {}` this override was inert
 on every path, so no real StateGraph ever compiled or ran; the
 coordinate now lives in top-level `:deps`, the actually-used path. (2)
 `forestrysupport.advisor` was a docstring-only skeleton with NO
 protocol and NO function, never `:require`d from `src/` -- completely
 dead code despite its own docstring's production claims; it is now a
 real `Advisor` protocol + `MockAdvisor`, genuinely consulted from the
 compiled graph's `:advise` node (proven in `operation-test.cljc` by
 swapping in custom `Advisor` implementations and observing the
 Governor's routing and the committed ledger record change accordingly
 -- not a hardcoded pass). (3) `forestrysupport.store`'s
 `log-service-record`/`mark-scheduled`/`append-fact` were called ONLY
 from `store-test.cljc`, never from any real execution path -- a new
 `Store` protocol + `MemStore` (atom-backed, composing those same pure
 functions) is now the actor's single mutable SSoT, closed over by
 `operation/build` and mutated ONLY from the compiled graph's real
 `:commit`/`:hold` nodes; `store-test.cljc` and `operation-test.cljc`
 both assert the ledger stays empty until a genuine commit/hold executes
 and that a governor-hold or a rejected approval NEVER touches the SSoT.

 `:itonami.blueprint/robotics` is honestly `false` -- this actor holds NO
 chainsaw/skidder/patrol-vehicle field-equipment-control authority (a
 HARD, permanent governor block, never overridable by human approval --
 see `forestrysupport.governor` ns docstring). ISIC Rev.5 0240 covers
 CONTRACT LOGGING-SUPPORT SERVICES for OTHER forest operators on a
 fee/contract basis -- timber cruising, forest-fire-protection support
 (patrol / fuel-break maintenance support, NOT firefighting/suppression
 itself), seed collection, transport of logs within the forest -- the
 operator never fells or owns the standing timber being serviced, which
 is what distinguishes this actor from actual timber-harvesting divisions
 (022x) themselves. Every one of its four proposal ops
 (`:log-service-record` / `:schedule-field-operation` /
 `:flag-forest-health-concern` / `:order-supplies`) carries `:effect
 :propose` ONLY -- the governor HARD-holds any proposal that doesn't
 (`effect-not-propose-violations`). Service types split into
 survey/collection (timber cruising, seed collection -- no
 field-equipment-operation safety window at all) and field-equipment-
 operation (forest-fire-protection support, in-forest log transport -- a
 genuine field-equipment-operator certification requirement, an
 equipment-inspection interval, and -- where physically applicable to
 that specific service -- a maximum fieldwork wind speed, a minimum
 riparian buffer, and a maximum haul-road load) -- the Governor's
 field-equipment-specific checks are skipped entirely, never fabricated,
 for survey/collection service types, and even within the
 field-equipment-operation category not every physical-constraint field
 applies to every service type (e.g. in-forest log transport has no
 fieldwork wind-speed ceiling of its own; fire-protection-support patrol/
 fuel-break work carries no haul-road load limit). `:log-service-record`
 and `:flag-forest-health-concern` always escalate to a human via the
 compiled graph's `:request-approval` node, regardless of advisor
 confidence; `:order-supplies` above a cost threshold likewise always
 escalates. This build ships NO JVM-only interop anywhere in `src/` (all
 source is `.cljc`) per this workspace's cljs-first runtime-priority
 rule. See `README.md` for the full governor-check enumeration."}
